{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-post-template-js","path":"/blog/2024-12-04-how-to-add-background-blur-in-react-using-css/","result":{"data":{"markdownRemark":{"excerpt":"Hi Friends 👋, Welcome To aHoisting! To add background blur in react using css, you can use  in . It will add background blur in react using css. Today, I am…","html":"<p>Hi Friends 👋,</p>\n<p>Welcome To aHoisting!</p>\n<p>To add background blur in react using css, you can use <code class=\"language-text\">backdrop-filter: blur(10px); -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(10px);</code> in <code class=\"language-text\">.blur-background</code>. It will add background blur in react using css.</p>\n<p>Today, I am going to show you, how to add background blur in react using css.</p>\n<p>Table of contents</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Install and create a new React app.</li>\n<li>Import react component.</li>\n<li>Create a Component.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Let’s start with the first step.</p>\n<h2>Step 1: Install and create a new React app.</h2>\n<p>First you have to install the React project. You should use <code class=\"language-text\">create-react-app</code> command to create a new React project.</p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"js\"><pre class=\"language-js\"><code class=\"language-js\">npx create<span class=\"token operator\">-</span>react<span class=\"token operator\">-</span>app my<span class=\"token operator\">-</span>app\ncd my<span class=\"token operator\">-</span>app\nnpm start</code></pre></div>\n<h2>Step 2: Import react component.</h2>\n<p>After installing, you have to import your React component.</p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"js\"><pre class=\"language-js\"><code class=\"language-js\"><span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> React <span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"token string\">\"react\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"token string\">\"./App.css\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span> </code></pre></div>\n<h2>Step 3: Create a Component.</h2>\n<p>You can use <code class=\"language-text\">className=\"blur-background\"</code> to add background blur in react using css.</p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"js\"><pre class=\"language-js\"><code class=\"language-js\"><span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span>div className<span class=\"token operator\">=</span><span class=\"token string\">\"app-container\"</span><span class=\"token operator\">></span>\n  <span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span>div className<span class=\"token operator\">=</span><span class=\"token string\">\"background-image\"</span><span class=\"token operator\">></span>\n        <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span><span class=\"token comment\">/* This is the underlying background */</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n  <span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span><span class=\"token operator\">/</span>div<span class=\"token operator\">></span>\n<span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span>div className<span class=\"token operator\">=</span><span class=\"token string\">\"blur-background\"</span><span class=\"token operator\">></span>\n  <span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span>h1<span class=\"token operator\">></span>Blurred Content<span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span><span class=\"token operator\">/</span>h1<span class=\"token operator\">></span>\n    <span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span><span class=\"token operator\">/</span>div<span class=\"token operator\">></span>\n<span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span><span class=\"token operator\">/</span>div<span class=\"token operator\">></span></code></pre></div>\n<h2>Add background blur example.</h2>\n<p>The below code is an example of a React. You have to import <code class=\"language-text\">react</code> and set <code class=\"language-text\">backdrop-filter: blur(10px); -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(10px);</code> in <code class=\"language-text\">.blur-background</code> to add background blur in react using css.</p>\n<p><code class=\"language-text\">App.js</code></p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"js\"><pre class=\"language-js\"><code class=\"language-js\"><span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> React <span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"token string\">\"react\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"token string\">\"./App.css\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span> \n\n<span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> <span class=\"token function-variable function\">App</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=></span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>\n    <span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span>div className<span class=\"token operator\">=</span><span class=\"token string\">\"app-container\"</span><span class=\"token operator\">></span>\n      <span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span>div className<span class=\"token operator\">=</span><span class=\"token string\">\"background-image\"</span><span class=\"token operator\">></span>\n        <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span><span class=\"token comment\">/* This is the underlying background */</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n      <span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span><span class=\"token operator\">/</span>div<span class=\"token operator\">></span>\n      <span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span>div className<span class=\"token operator\">=</span><span class=\"token string\">\"blur-background\"</span><span class=\"token operator\">></span>\n        <span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span>h1<span class=\"token operator\">></span>Blurred Content<span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span><span class=\"token operator\">/</span>h1<span class=\"token operator\">></span>\n      <span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span><span class=\"token operator\">/</span>div<span class=\"token operator\">></span>\n    <span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span><span class=\"token operator\">/</span>div<span class=\"token operator\">></span>\n  <span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"token keyword\">export</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">default</span> App<span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span></code></pre></div>\n<p><code class=\"language-text\">App.css</code></p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"css\"><pre class=\"language-css\"><code class=\"language-css\"><span class=\"token selector\">.app-container</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"token property\">height</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">:</span> 100vh<span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"token property\">display</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">:</span> flex<span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"token property\">align-items</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">:</span> center<span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"token property\">justify-content</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">:</span> center<span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"token property\">background-image</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">:</span> <span class=\"token url\"><span class=\"token function\">url</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string url\">\"./beautiful-nature.jpeg\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span> <span class=\"token comment\">/* Background image */</span>\n  <span class=\"token property\">background-size</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">:</span> cover<span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"token property\">background-position</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">:</span> center<span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"token selector\">.blur-background</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"token property\">width</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">:</span> 80%<span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"token property\">padding</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">:</span> 20px<span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"token property\">backdrop-filter</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">:</span> <span class=\"token function\">blur</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>10px<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"token property\">-webkit-backdrop-filter</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">:</span> <span class=\"token function\">blur</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>10px<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"token property\">background-color</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">:</span> <span class=\"token function\">rgba</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>255<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> 255<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> 255<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> 0.3<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"token property\">border-radius</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">:</span> 10px<span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n  <span class=\"token property\">text-align</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">:</span> center<span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>In the above code example, I have used the <code class=\"language-text\">backdrop-filter: blur(10px); -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(10px);</code> to add background blur in react using css.</p>\n<p>Check the output of the above code.</p>\n<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 630px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/f0fcaadc557e3a81a306e038f142dc28/87c73/background-blur.webp\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 50%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/webp;base64,UklGRo4AAABXRUJQVlA4IIIAAAAQBACdASoUAAoAPtFUo0uoJKMhsAgBABoJaACdMoAC/3qzssooYAl+gAD+Pam1z1v8JwEDAhPk+j+VVdesO8y6k/XSzpEVA0dD65nTkUAqc+zwLK3wR/FWrLS4dgU+gODhaZ3sLvSWmoq/4OeIno7maigMLgTjG0Lyf2F3wS3M1TwA'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        alt=\"React, background, blur\"\n        title=\"React, background, blur\"\n        src=\"/static/f0fcaadc557e3a81a306e038f142dc28/8aab1/background-blur.webp\"\n        srcset=\"/static/f0fcaadc557e3a81a306e038f142dc28/81b7c/background-blur.webp 158w,\n/static/f0fcaadc557e3a81a306e038f142dc28/6ea66/background-blur.webp 315w,\n/static/f0fcaadc557e3a81a306e038f142dc28/8aab1/background-blur.webp 630w,\n/static/f0fcaadc557e3a81a306e038f142dc28/a70f5/background-blur.webp 945w,\n/static/f0fcaadc557e3a81a306e038f142dc28/4ef06/background-blur.webp 1260w,\n/static/f0fcaadc557e3a81a306e038f142dc28/87c73/background-blur.webp 1353w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 630px) 100vw, 630px\"\n        style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n        loading=\"lazy\"\n        decoding=\"async\"\n      />\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p>All the best 👍</p>","frontmatter":{"title":"How to add background blur in react using css?","tags":["React"],"date":"December 04, 2024","description":"Example of add background blur in react using css with step by step tutorial - aHoisting","social_image":{"absolutePath":"/Users/mac/Documents/hoisting/ahoisting/static/media/template/reactjs.jpg"}}},"prev":{"frontmatter":{"title":"How to create horizontal line in react js?"},"fields":{"slug":"/blog/2024-12-05-how-to-create-horizontal-line-in-react-js/"}},"next":{"frontmatter":{"title":"How to add black overlay on image in react using  css?"},"fields":{"slug":"/blog/2024-12-04-how-to-add-black-overlay-on-image-in-react-using-css/"}}},"pageContext":{"slug":"/blog/2024-12-04-how-to-add-background-blur-in-react-using-css/","prevSlug":"/blog/2024-12-05-how-to-create-horizontal-line-in-react-js/","nextSlug":"/blog/2024-12-04-how-to-add-black-overlay-on-image-in-react-using-css/"}},"staticQueryHashes":["2555585279","2714594843","3159585216"]}